Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/libtests/makepng.c
Line: 1199
Function: insert_iCCP
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: When handling a fake iCCP profile, the code writes a 4-byte length field into the start of the allocated buffer via png_save_uint_32(profile, proflen) without ensuring the buffer is at least 4 bytes long. If fake_len < 4, the buffer allocated by load_fake is smaller than 4 bytes, leading to a 1–3 byte write past the end of the heap buffer.

Source context:
```c
